I find these comments very interesting.

My personal view (aired previously in detail on this group) is that the
early game is by far the most fun and the game gets progressively more
boring as you go on.  What I enjoy about the early game is that the
differentiation between the classes makes a huge difference to how you
approach each situation.  In the late game, every character regardless
of class gets closer and closer to the ideal "ascendable" character (ie
maxed stats, MR, MC, AC -30 odd, a few useful spells, artefact weapon,
the usual armour set, etc).  Thus the mid/late game is the same
regardless of what character you start with, and I find the
repetitiveness boring.

I guess a large part of nethack's appeal is that different people get
particular enjoyment from different parts of the game (although of
course there are parts which are almost universally disliked, like
Gehennom).

